From: harunkkhan <harunkkhan1@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Start the macOS notification service on first use

Chrome starts each notification dispatcher's service at launch so that macOS
asks for notification permission on Chrome's first start (crbug.com/40149365).
The embedder asks when a page first shows a notification instead: every other
entry point returns early while no service runs, and DisplayNotification starts
it.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/notifications/mac/notification_dispatcher_mojo.cc b/chrome/browser/notifications/mac/notification_dispatcher_mojo.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/notifications/mac/notification_dispatcher_mojo.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/notifications/mac/notification_dispatcher_mojo.cc
@@ -40,12 +40,7 @@
 NotificationDispatcherMojo::NotificationDispatcherMojo(
     std::unique_ptr<MacNotificationProviderFactory> provider_factory)
     : provider_factory_(std::move(provider_factory)),
-      next_service_restart_timer_delay_(kInitialServiceRestartTimerDelay) {
-  // Force start the notification service once so we show the permission request
-  // to users on the first start of Chrome.
-  // TODO(crbug.com/40149365): Find a better time to ask for permissions.
-  CheckIfServiceCanBeTerminated();
-}
+      next_service_restart_timer_delay_(kInitialServiceRestartTimerDelay) {}
 
 NotificationDispatcherMojo::~NotificationDispatcherMojo() = default;
 
